    "ls|LS16_S8_U_170": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *170 (10 th  Position)  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 5-5-2016  \n \nSolid and Liquid Waste Management \n \n*170. SHRI KALIKESH N. SINGH DEO: \nMOHAMMED FAIZAL: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the financial and technical assistance provided to State Governments for Solid and Liquid Waste \nManagement (SLWM) as part of the Swachh Bharat Mission (SBM ) during each of the last three \nyears and the current year, State-wise; \n \n(b) whether the Government has conducted workshops with State Governm ents to issue guidelines \non SLWM, if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to provide more financial ass istance to States and UTs under \nSLWM and if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  \n(SHRI BIRENDER SINGH) \n \n \n \n(a) to (c) A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.  *170 for 05.05.2016. \n \n(a) Under Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) SBM-G, there is a p rovision of assistance of up to Rs. \n7/12/15/20 lakh for Gram Panchayats with 150/300/500/more than 500 households. Regar ding \ntechnical assistance to States, exhibitions and workshop are held  at regular intervals to disseminate \nvarious innovative technologies & best practices among the State s for adoption. Besides, Solid and \nLiquid Waste Management (SLWM) guidelines within the SBM(G) Guidelines, the Ministry has \nfurther shared Guidelines on Solid and Liquid Waste Management (SLWM ) and A Source Book on \nSLWM in Rural Areas with States in the last three years to help the States to take-up SLWM \nProjects. Under SBM-G, component-wise funds are not released. Howe ver,  State/UT-wise central \nshare released under Nirmal Bharat Abhiyaan (NBA)/SBM (G) du ring the last 3 years and the \ncurrent year is at Annexure-1. \n(b) Three regional workshops were organized at Trivandrum, Guwahati and Ranchi during 2014-15. \nA National workshop on SLWM was organized in New Delhi on 21.04.2015. Thre e Exhibitions \nwere organized in New Delhi on 26-27 th  August 2014, 23-24 January 2015 and 2-3 July 2015 \nwherein  innovative technologies in respect of Solid and Liquid Waste M anagement were \nshowcased to various State Governments.    \n(c) Under SBM-G, component-wise funds are not released. However, St ate/UT may take-up \nSLWM projects as per SBM(G) Guidelines. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-1 \nStatement referred in part (a) of the reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.170 due for reply on 5-\n05-2016 \nState/UT-wise, Central share released during last 3 years and current year under NBA / SBM(G) \n(Rs. in Crore) \nState/UT 2013-14 2014-15 2015- 16                               2016-17(Upto \n30-4-2016)                               \nA & N ILANDS 0 0 3.40   \nANDHRA PRADESH  145.24 116.10 234.17   \nARUNACHAL PRADESH  5.19 14.61 38.71 4.73 \nASSAM  41.81 185.78 187.67   \nBIHAR  0.00 0.00 182.14   \nCHHATTISGARH  0.00 28.12 144.72 77.96 \nD & N HAVELI  0.00 0.00 0.00   \nGOA  0.00 0.00 1.05   \nGUJARAT  52.64 156.07 478.22   \nHARYANA  131.18 5.93 29.53   \nHIMACHAL PRADESH  30.50 130.17 4.37   \nJAMMU & KASHMIR  39.57 103.08 4.05   \nJHARKHAND  0.00 23.05 97.32 81.18 \nKARNATAKA  65.95 312.57 335.45   \nKERALA  43.01 33.97 8.50   \nMADHYA PRADESH  660.39 0.00 220.28   \nMAHARASHTRA  36.46 236.11 567.45   \nMANIPUR  0.00 9.18 44.19 27.27 \nMEGHALAYA  103.04 0.00 35.65 41.22 \nMIZORAM  8.06 0.00 3.32   \nNAGALAND  0.00 20.87 10.83   \nODISHA  0.00 65.84 566.50 359.37 \nPUDUCHERRY  0.00 2.00 0.00   \nPUNJAB  0.00 0.00 23.90 19.46 \nRAJASTHAN  0.00 271.57 938.73 491.60 \nSIKKIM  8.25 3.89 6.12 4.81 \nTAMIL NADU  311.92 205.12 78.94 210.42 \nTELANGANA