    "ls|LS16_S8_U_218": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION No. *218\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 09.05.2016\n \n \nREGISTRATION OF MSME\n \n \n*218. \n \nSHRI PONGULETI SRINIVASA REDDY:\n \n \n \nSHRI KALIKESH N. SINGH DEO: \n \n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be \npleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the fourth All India Census of Micro, Small and Medium \nEnterprises (MSMEs) has revealed that the registration rate of MSMEs has \nshown a declining trend, if so, the \ndetails thereof and reasons therefor;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the Government proposes to use Udyog Aadhaar for online \nregistration of the MSMEs in the country, if so, the details thereof along with \nthe number of MSMEs registered/filed entrepreneur memorandum during \nthe \nlast year, State/UT\n-\nwise;\n \n \n(c)\n \n \nwhether the Government proposes to establish an apex body for \nuniversal registration of the MSMEs in the country, if so, the details thereof; \nand\n \n \n(d)\n \n \nthe other measures taken/being taken by the Government to encourage \nand improve the registration of MSMEs in the country including making \nregistration mandatory?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \n(SHRI KALRAJ MISHRA)\n \n \n(a)to(d):\n \n \nA statement is laid down on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT \nREFFERED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) IN \nRESPECT OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *218 FOR \nANSWER ON 09\n-\n05\n-\n2016\n \n \n \n(a):\n \nNo, Madam.  The registration of the working MSMEs has been \nincreasing over a period of time. As per the 4\nth\n \nCensus, the total number \nof \nregistered MSME units was 22.48 lakhs (15.64 lakh units working and \nremaining ones closed or untraceable) whereas as per 3\nrd\n \nCensus,  the total \nnumber of SSI units permanently registered up to 31\nst\n \nMarch, 2001 was 22.62 \nlakhs (13.75 lakh units working a\nnd remaining ones closed).   \n \n \n \n(b):\n \nYes,  Madam.  \nThe Ministry on 18\n-\n09\n-\n15 has notified for online filing of \nUdyog Aadhaar Memorandum (UAM) at \nhttp://udyogaadhaar.gov.in\n \nby \nMSMEs.  In order to promote e\nase of doing business for MSMEs, Government \nhas simplified the registration process of MSMEs through\n \nUAM.  Cumbersome \nprocess of filing Entrepreneurs Memorandum Part \n–\nII (EM\n-\nII) has been \nreplaced with a one\n-\n \npage, simplified online UAM form.  No fee is req\nuired for \nfiling of UAM.  UAM is filed on self\n-\ndeclaration basis and no documentation is \nrequired. Number of EM\n-\nII filed during 2015\n-\n16 are 2,17,854. From 18.9.2015 \nto 31.03.2016, 500058 units filed UAM. The State/UT\n-\nwise details are placed at \nAnnexure\n-\nI. \n \n \n \n(c):\n \nNo, Madam. \n \n \n \n(d)\n:  \n \nThe filing of UAM is voluntary.  State Government and industry \nassociations have been urged by Government of India to expedite the pace of \nregistration of UAM through a series of communications, interactive sessions \nover video\n-\nconferencing and holding Regional Conclaves. Banks and Financial \nInstitutions have also been sensitized about acceptance of UAM at par with EM\n-\nII.   \n \n \n   \n \n******\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nAnnexure Referred to in Reply to part(b) of Lok Sabha\n \nStarred Question No. \n*218 due for answer on 09\n-\n05\n-\n2016\n \nMSMEs Registered in 2015\n-\n16 ( EM\n-\nIIs and UAMs filed )\n \n \nS.No. \n \nName of State/UT\n \nNumber of \nEM\n-\nII filed\n \nTotal No of \nUAMs filed\n \nTotal \nnumber of  \nregistrations\n \n1\n \nANDHRA PRADESH\n \n3677\n \n9792\n \n13469\n \n2\n \nARUNACHAL PRADESH\n \n0\n \n61\n \n61\n \n3\n \nASSAM\n \n1075\n \n38\n \n1113\n \n4\n \nBIHAR\n \n345\n \n98738\n \n99083\n \n5\n \nCHHATTISGARH\n \n665\n \n4761\n \n5426\n \n6\n \nGOA\n \n49\n \n791\n \n840\n \n7\n \nGUJARAT\n \n36616\n \n52053\n \n88669