    "ls|LS16_S8_U_247": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.247 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 26TH APRIL, 2016/VAISAKHA 6, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nRELEASE OF UNDERTRIALS \n \n247.    DR. SHASHI THAROOR: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that a total of  12,052 undertrials have been \ndetained for a  period of more than three years in various  jails in the \ncountry; \n \n(b) if so, whether the Government has  been working in coordination with \nthe National Legal Services Authority (NLSA) for their timely release and if \nso, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Supreme Court had  directed the State Legal Services \nAuthority (SLSA) to secure the release of the  undertrials who have served \nhalf of the apprehended term; \n \n(d) if so, w hether the Government has  been co-ordinating with the SLSAs \nto ensure that they are complying with the directive; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof including  the total number of undertrials who \nhave been released during each of the last three  years and the current \nyear, State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HARIBHAI PARATHIBHAI CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a):  As per data compiled by the National Crime Records Bureau at the \nend of 2014, t he total number of undertrials between 3 to  5 years was \n12052 in the jails of the country. \n….2/ \n\n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.247 FOR 26.04.2016 \n(b) to (d): In pursuant to the directions of Hon’ble Supreme Court of India \nin Writ Petition No. 406 of 2013 titled Re -Inhuman Conditions prevailing in \n1382 Prisons, al l the State Legal Services Authorities (SLSAs) had been \nrequested by National Legal Services Authority (NALSA) to urgently take \nup the case of the undertrial prisoners who are entitled to the benefit of \nSection 436-A of Cr.P.C. and to instruct the panel lawyers to urgently meet \nsuch prisoners and move appropriate application before the Courts for \ntheir release. Further, pursuant to the directions of Hon’ble Supreme \nCourt, Under Trial Review Committee has been established in every \ndistrict across the country comprising of District Judges as Chairman and \nSecretary, District Legal Services Authorities as one of the members to \nmonitor and review the cases of aforesaid under -trial prisoners of their \nearly release. \n \n(e): On the basis of the reports received from various State Legal \nServices Authorities (SLSAs) and provided by NALSA, a  statement \ncontaining the information of Under Trial Prisoners released pursuant to \nthe directions of Hon’ble Supreme Court of India since 1st July, 2015 to 31st \nJanuary, 2016 is at Annexure. \n********    \n\nPAGE 1 OF 1 OF ANNEXURE \n \nAnnexure referred to in part (e) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question  \nNo. 247 for answer on 26.4.2016 \n \n****** \nS. No. State/UT No. of Undertrial Prisoners released pursuant to \nthe directions of Hon’ble Supreme Court of India \nsince 1st July 2015 to 31st January 2016 \n1 Andhra Pradesh 43 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 09 \n3 Assam Nil \n4 Bihar 42 \n5 Chhattisgarh 19 \n6 Goa Nil \n7 Gujarat 06 \n8 Haryana Nil \n9 Himachal Pradesh Nil \n10 Jammu & Kashmir Data not available \n11 Jharkhand 30 \n12 Karnataka 39 \n13 Kerala 26 \n14 Madhya Pradesh -- \n15 Maharashtra 4923 \n16 Manipur 02 \n17 Meghalaya 107 \n18 Mizoram None \n19 Nagaland Nil \n20 Odisha 24 \n21 Punjab 84 \n22 Rajasthan 69 \n23 Sikkim Nil \n24 Tamil Nadu 133 \n25 Telangana 24 \n26 Tripura 41 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 198 \n28 Uttarakhand Nil  \n29 West Bengal Nil \n30 A & N Islands None \n31 Chandigarh Nil \n32 D & N Haveli Nil \n33 Daman & Diu Nil \n34 Delhi 157 applications recommended by the UTRC to \nmove bail application \n35 Lakshadweep No prisoners in the jails \n36 Puducherry Nil ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_248": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \n  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 248 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MAY 11, 2016 \n \n \nPROMOTION OF RENTAL HOUSING \n \nNo. 248* SHRIMATI  K.MARAGATHAM: \nSHRI KALIKESH N. SINGH DEO: \n \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AN D URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n \n(a) whether the Government has undertaken measures to \npromote  rental housing in ur ban areas, if so, the details \nthereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(b) whether hostels, paying guest accommodations,  \ndormitories and single r oom sets for economically \nweaker section category are proposed to be constructed \nunder the National Urban R ental Housing Scheme and if \nso, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the said Rental Polic y provides fiscal and non-\nfiscal incentives to tenants, if so, the details thereof and \nif not, the reasons therefor; \n \n \n……contd./-\n \n\n-2- \n \n(d) whether measures have been  undertaken for fast   \nadjudication of rental disput es and if so, the details \nthereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) the steps taken to firm up in novative rental housing   \nmodels? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF HOUSING & URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n \n(SHRI M. VENKAIAH NAIDU) \n \n \n(a) to (e):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the Sabha. \n \n \n \n  \n\n-3- \nSTATEMENT \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.  248  FOR 11.5.2016  REGARDING PROMOTION OF \nRENTAL HOUSING \n \n(a)     :  National Urban Housing and Habitat Policy, 2007 \nadvocates creating adeq uate housing stock both on \nrental and ownershi p basis, with special emphasis on \nimproving the affordability of the vulnerable and \neconomically weaker sections of society. \n \nMinistry of Housing and Ur ban Poverty Alleviation has \nprepared a draft National Ur ban Rental Housing Policy \n(NURHP). This focuses on adoption of a multi-pronged \napproach with supply as well as demand side \ninterventions and encourage involvement of Private \nSector, Cooperative, Non-Governmental Sector, Industrial \nand the Services/Institutional Sector, to promote rental \nhousing. \n \n(b)     : There is no National R ental Housing Scheme at present.  \n \n(c)     :   The Draft NURHP outlines certain recommendatory \nincentives, both fiscal and non- fiscal which include relief \nin certain taxation, stamp duty and registration charges, \nprovision of rental voucher s, encouraging investment for \nimproving rental housing stock etc. \n \n(d)   :     ‘Land’ and ‘Colonisation ’ being state subjects, it is up to \nState Governments to resolve rental disputes.  In order to \nfacilitate the State Governments, Ministry of Housing and \nUrban Poverty Alleviation has shared a draft Model \nTenancy Act, with the objective to establish a framework \nfor the regulation of Te nancy for commercial and \nresidential properties; balance the rights and \nresponsibilities of landlords and tenants through rental  \n \n……contd./- \n\n \n \n-4- \n  \n \n      contracts; ensure regis tration of rental contracts with \nRent Authorities; establish fast adjudication process for \nresolution of disputes through Rent Tribunals, etc. It is \nupto States/Union Territories to adopt the provisions of \nthis Model Act.  \n \n(e)    :   The Draft NURHP envisages that the respective \nStates/Union Territories will develop their own models on \nrental housing as per the local need and demand/supply \nmechanisms of the housing market. \n \n********* \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_249": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY DAIRYING & FISHERIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.  249. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 26th April 2016 \nRASHTRIYA GOKUL MISSION  \n249. SHRI RAJENDRA AGRAWAL  \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE :   कृ षि औरकृ िक कल्याण मंत्री \nbe pleased to state \n(a) the details of the outlay under Rashtriya Gokul Mission during the 12th Five Year \nPlan period;  \n(b)  the details of funds budgeted, released and utilized so far for the said scheme, \nState/UT-wise including Uttar Pradesh;  \n(c)  the details of proposed Integrated Indigenous Cattle Center or Gokul Grams and \nMetropolitan Gokul Grams operationalized so far, State /UT-wise including Uttar \nPradesh;  \n(d)  whether incidences related to outbreak of animal diseases have been reported from \nGokul Grams so far; and \n (e)  if so, the details thereof, State/ UT -wise including Uttar Pradesh along with the \ncorrective steps taken by the Government thereon? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \n(SHRI MOHANBHAI KUNDARIYA) \n(a): Rashtriya Gokul Mission has been initiated with an allocation of Rs 500 crores \nduring the remaining three years of the 12th Plan period from 2014-15. \n(b): The details of the funds budgeted, released  and utilized so far for the said \nscheme, State/UT-wise including Uttar Pradesh is given in Annexure-I. \n (c): The integrated cattle development centres are being established in the State of \nAndhra Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Gujarat, Haryana, Madhya Prades h, \nMaharashtra, Nagaland, Odisha , Punjab, Rajasthan, Telangana and Uttar \nPradesh. \n (d) & (e): No, Madam. Question does not arise.  \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nStatement referred to in reply to part ( b) of Lok Sabha unstarred Question No.  \n249 for 26.04.2016 \n \nFunds Released for implementation of Rashtriya Gokul Mission under National \nProgramme for Bovine Breeding & Indigenous breeds  \nRs in lakh \nS. No State  2014-15 Funds \nUtilized \n2015-16 Funds \nUtilized \n1 Andhra Pradesh 400.00 100.00     \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 0.00 0.00 111.00 0.00 \n3 Assam  150.00 0.00     \n4 Bihar 0.00   350.00 0.00 \n5 Chhattisgarh  729.00 500.00     \n6 Gujarat 0.00 0.00 803.22 0.00 \n7 Haryana 200.00 0.00     \n8 Himachal Pradesh  350.00 0.00     \n9 Jammu & Kashmir 0.00   25.00 0.00 \n10 Jharkhand 35.00 35.00     \n11 Karnataka 0.00 0.00 60.00 0.00 \n12 Kerala 250.00 250.00 400.00   \n13 Madhya Pradesh 2000.00 1840.00 1881.50 1881.50 \n14 Maharashtra 100.00 100.00     \n15 Manipur 450.00 450.00 280.02 100.00 \n16 Mizoram 0.00 0.00 50.45 0.00 \n17 Nagaland 448.00 448.00 350.10 125.00 \n18 Odisha 856.00 856.00     \n19 Punjab 0.00 0.00 600.00 0.00 \n20 Rajasthan 300.00 0.00     \n21 Sikkim 450.00 0.00   0.00 \n22 Tamil Nadu 1776.00 0.00   0.00 \n23 Telangana 300.00 0.00   0.00 \n24 Tripura 417.00 0.00   0.00 \n25 UP 800.00 800.00 200.00 0.00 \n26 Uttarakhand 500.00 387.00   0.00 \n27 West Bengal 0.00 0.00 480.28 0.00 \n  Total 10511.00 5766.00 5591.57 2106.50 \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_25": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.25 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 \n \nSchool of Planning and Architecture \n \n†25. SHRI GOPAL SHETTY:  \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has received proposals from the State Government of \nMaharashtra for establishing School of Planning and Architecture (SPA) at \nAurangabad and for reimbursement o f expenditure by Central Government incurred \non Sixth Pay Commission for teachers and subsequent cadres in the State; \n(b) if so, the details thereof at present; and  \n(c) the time by which it is proposed to be finalised and the reasons for delay taking \nplace in this regard? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a): Yes Madam.  \n(b) and (c): As of now, there is no proposal to establish a School of Planning and \nArchitecture in the State of Maharashtra.  In so far as reimbursement of expenditure \nby Central Government incurred on Sixth Pay Commission for teachers is \nconcerned, the Ministry had received a proposal from the State Government of \nMaharashtra for reimbursement of Rs.1470,21,30,487 (80% of the am ount of \nRs.1837,76,63,109/-) as total central share for payment of salary arrears on account \nof implementation of the revised UGC pay scales, for the period 1.1.2006 to \n31.03.2010. However, as per the undertaking submitted by the State Government \nvide letter dated 21.05.2013, an amount of Rs.1150,16,00,000/ - had actually been \ndisbursed by the State Government, out of which the centr al share of \nRs.920,12,80,000/- (80% of total paid amount) has been released to the State \nGovernment of Maharashtra in six (6) installments.  \n \n******************* ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_26": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.26 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 26.04.2016 \n \nImpact of Microbeads on Environment \n \n26. SHRI DHANANJAY MAHADIK: \n      SHRI SATAV RAJEEV: \n \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FORESTS AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  whether all leading brands including herbal brands are reportedly using microbeads for \n manufacturing soap, toothpaste and other products causing adverse impact on \n environment; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and reaction of the Government thereto; \n(c)  whether the National Green Tribunal has issued notices to the Ministries of Environment, \n Forests and Climate Change; Water Resources and Health and Family Welfare seeking \n their comments on the use of microbeads in personal care products; \n(d)  if so, the details thereof along with the response thereon; and \n(e)  the other corrective steps taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND \nCLIMATE CHANGE  \n \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a)&(b)   According to the Central Drug Standard s Control Organization, it has not received any \nreport of adverse impact on environment regarding use of microbeads for manufacturing soap, \ntoothpaste and other products. However, existing regulations under Schedule S of the Drugs and \nCosmetics Rules, 1945, prescribe that Cosmetics in finished form shall conform to the Bureau of \nIndian Standards (BIS) specificatio ns laid down from time to time by the BIS.    Ministry of \nEnvironment, Forest and Climate Change has not commissioned any study to ascertain the \nextent and type of microbeads being used for manufacturing soap, toothpaste and other products \nand their impact on environment.  \n \n(c)   Yes, Madam. \n \n(d)   The National Green Tribunal (NGT) in the matter of O.A. No.112/2016, Ashwini Kumar \nVs Union of India & Others, issued notices to the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate \nChange; Ministry of Water Resources, Ri ver Development and Ganga Rejuvenation and \nMinistry of Health and Family Welfare seeking responses. The Ministry has already initiated \naction to file reply to the NGT.  \n \n(e)   Since no study has been carried out on the matter, no corrective steps have been taken. \n \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_27": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.27 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 \n \nTwelfth Class Board Exams \n27. DR. C. GOPALAKRISHNAN: \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Government is aware of the fact that many students particularly \ngirls who appeared in 12th class CBSE exams faced difficulty due to lengthy and out \nof syllabus questions asked in the exams etc. and are being led to commit suicide \nand if so, the details thereof ;  \n(b) the total number of such cases reported during the last three years, State/ UT -\nwise;  \n(c) the suitable measures taken/ proposed to be taken by the Government to avoid \nsuch situations in future; and  \n(d) whether the Government has formed any Committee in this regard especially to \nanalyse the question pattern in Board exams and if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a) : There have been new spaper reports on the issue during the Board exam  of \n2016.  The question papers are  based on curriculum, syllabus and sample question \npapers prescribed by the Board.   CBSE has informed that it is not aware of suicide \ncommitted by any student of its affil iated schools due to the lengthy and out of \nsyllabus question paper for Board Exam, 2016. \n(b) : CBSE has informed that it does not maintain data on suicides by students in \naffiliated schools.   \n(c) & (d) : CBSE has a well established mechanism of subject- wise committees for \nanalysis the syllabus and question paper patterns on continuous basis.  \n \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_28": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 28 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 \n \nVedic Education \n \n†28. SHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to constitute any Managing Committee for promoting \nVedic Maths and Sanskrit; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to make Vedic Maths and Sanskrit as compulsory \nsubjects at primary level in the country; and \n \n(d) if so, the time by which the said plan is likely to be implemented? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a) No such proposal under consideration.   \n \n(b)  Does not arise. \n \n(c)  No such proposal under consideration. \n \n(d) Does not arise. \n \n****** ",
