    "ls|LS16_S8_U_74": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 74 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.04.2016 \n \nUnrest among Students of NIT \n \n74. SHRI JYOTIRADITYA M. SCINDIA: \n SHRI KAMAL NATH: \n SHRI LALLU SINGH:  \n SHRI VENKATESH BABU T.G.: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware of the unrest among students of National \nInstitute of Technology(NIT), Srinagar;  \n(b)  if so, the reasons therefor and the demands of the students made in this regard;  \n(c)  whether the Government has sent a team of the Ministry to resolve the crisis \nbeing witnessed for the last few days;  \n(d)  if so, the details of the recommendations made by the team of  the Ministry and \nthe outcome thereof; and  \n(e)  the steps taken by the Government to instill confidence among students in the \ncampus, especially to provide sense of security to girl students? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a) to (e) : Yes, Madam. A communication  was received in the Ministry from \nNational Institute of Technology  (NIT), Srinagar (Jammu and Kashmir)  on 01 st \nApril, 2016 regarding student unrest due to the confrontation between two groups \nof students of NIT, Srinagar which took place on 01st April, 2016. Subsequently, it \nwas reported that J&K Police lathi charged agitating students of NIT, Srinagar on \n5th April, 2016.  The major demand of the students was to shift the NIT out of \nSrinagar. The Ministry of Human Resource Development had sent its team to \ntake stock of the situation. Adequate Security Forces have been deployed to \nprovide a sense of security to the students including girl students. \n*-*-*-*-*-* ",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_75": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nDEPAERTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 75\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 28.04.2016\nCLASSIFICATION OF BPL FAMILIES\n*75 . COL. SONARAM CHOUDHARY:\nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has issued guidelines to the State Governments to identify\nfamilies Below Poverty Line (BPL) category, if so, the details thereof;\n(b) whether different criteria is being followed by various State Governments for\nidentifying people under BPL, and if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether there are allegations that Panchayati Raj Institutions like Gram Samities have\nbeen partial in including the non-eligible people under the BPL category and if so, the\ndetails thereof; and\n(d) whether the Government proposes to issue directions/instructions to all the State\nGovernments to streamline the process of identification of BPL families with a view\nto safeguard the interest of the poorest among the poor people?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT\n(SHRI BIRENDER SINGH)\n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n*****\n\nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.75 for answer on 28th\nApril, 2016.\n(a), (b) & (d): The Ministry of Rural Development provides financial and technical support\nto the States/UTs for conducting Socio Economic and Caste Census -2011 (SECC -2011) to\ngenerate a large number of socio and economic indicators for ranking of households across\nthe country. Ranking of Households is made through a three -step process involving thirteen\nExclusion parameters for identifying not -poor households, five Automatic Inclusion\nparameters for identifying poorest of the poor households and seven Deprivation Criteri a for\nidentifying poor households.  Government of India has advised states to use this process and\nSECC data for identification of poor households under Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana (DAY)\nand Pradhan Mantri  Aawaas  Yojana(PMAY).\n(c): The Socio Economic and Caste Census 2011 used canvasser method to elicit information\non questionnaire directly from each of the households and not through Gram Samities.",
    "ls|LS16_S8_U_76": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *76 (16 th  Position)  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 28-4-2016  \n \nSanitary Complexes \n \n*76. SHRI KESINENI NANI: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the funds generated through Swachh Bharat Cess so far, State-wise; \n \n(b) the criteria/structure for disbursal of these funds/cess to the States/UTs; \n \n(c) the financial assistance provided to various State Governm ents including Andhra Pradesh under \nSwachh Bharat Mission (SBM) during each of the last three yea rs and the current year, State/UT-\nwise; \n \n(d) the steps taken for total sanitation of villages through the c onstruction of drains soaked pits, \nsolid and liquid waste disposal under SBM in Andhra Pradesh; and \n \n(e) the number of sanitary complexes for women with facilitie s for sanitation, bathing and washing \nconstructed in Andhra Pradesh under SBM? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  \n(SHRI BIRENDER SINGH) \n \n \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.  *76 for 28.4.2016. \n \n(a) The total amount collected under Swachh Bharat Cess (SBC) dur ing mid-November 2015 to \nMarch 2016 is Rs. 3900 crore (provisional gross figure). The State-w ise data in this regard is not \nmaintained by Central Board of Excise & Customs, Department of Revenue.  \n \n(b) \nFunds collected under the Cess will be distributed between the tw o Sub-Missions i.e. Swachh \nBharat Mission (Gramin) and Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) in the ratio of 80:20 respectively and \nutilized as per the guidelines and components of Swachh Bharat Mis sion (Gramin) and Swachh \nBharat Mission (Urban).  \n \n(c) State/UT-wise, Central share released during last 3 ye ars and current year  to various State \nGovernments including Andhra Pradesh under Nirmal Bharat Abhiyan (NBA ) (upto 1 st  October, \n2014) / Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) (from 2 nd  October, 2014) is at Annexure-1.  State/UT-\nwise, Central share released during last 3 years and current y ear  to various State Governments \nincluding Andhra Pradesh under Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) is at Annexure-2. \n \n(d) The Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) has been launched on 2nd Octob er, 2014, which aims at \nattaining Swachh Bharat by 2 nd  October 2019. Solid and Liquid Waste Management (SLWM) is \none of the integral component of SBM(G) and under this component, activi ties like compost pits, \nvermi composting, biogas plants, low cost drainage, soakage channel s/ pits, reuse of waste water \nand system for collection, , segregation and disposal of household garbag e and menstrual hygiene \nmanagement etc. can be taken up. Funds for Solid and Liquid Waste Ma nagement activities with \ncap of Rs. 7/12/15/20 lakh are available for Gram Panchayats having upto 150/300/500/ more than \n500 households.  \n \n(e) 10  Community Sanitary Complexes have been constructed in Andhra Prades h under Swachh \nBharat Mission(Gramin) since 2.10.2014.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-1 \nStatement referred in part (d) of the reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.76 due for reply on 28-\n04-2016 \nState/UT-wise, Central share released during last 3 years and current year under NBA / SBM(G)* \n(Rs. in Crore) \nState/UT 2013-14 2014-15 2015- 16                               2016-17(Upto \n25-4-2016)                               \nA & N ILANDS 0 0 3.40   \nANDHRA PRADESH  145.24 116.10 234.17   \nARUNACHAL PRADESH  5.19 14.61 38.71 4.73 \nASSAM  41.81 185.78 187.67   \nBIHAR  0.00 0.00 182.14   \nCHHATTISGARH  0.00 28.12 144.72 77.96 \nD & N HAVELI  0.00 0.00 0.00   \nGOA  0.00 0.00 1.05   \nGUJARAT  52.64 156.07 478.22   \nHARYANA  131.18 5.93 29.53   \nHIMACHAL PRADESH  30.50 130.17 4.37   \nJAM